     "description": "The physics_update law at the convect_deep call site (proc zm_conv_tend, physpkg.F90 tphysbc), step 24, pinned from cam_phys_tend.csv / cam_phys_tend_q.csv rows (step 24, site convect_deep, lev 1..32, all 9 constituents) with the expected values chained to the next call site's dump rows (step 24, site convect_shallow: state_before(convect_shallow) == state_after(convect_deep), verified for the whole 48-step window at 1e-16 relative). Exercises: the T update T + ptend_s*dt/cpairv (cpairv = cpair, dry_air_species = ''), the u/v updates, the constituent updates with the qneg3 clamp (qmin = 1e-12 for Q, 0 for CLDLIQ/CLDICE/RAINQM/SNOWQM) and the number-concentration clamp min(max(q,1e-12),1e10) for NUMICE/NUMLIQ/NUMRAI/NUMSNO (fires at NUMICE across the column, e.g. lev 1: q_before = 9.999999899e-13 -> q_after = 1e-12 exactly), the state_cnst_min_nz(1e-36) zeroing of CLDLIQ/NUMLIQ and CLDICE/NUMICE (fires at CLDLIQ on ~29 of 32 levels, e.g. lev 1: q_before = 2.39688771960016664e-252 -> 0.0; and does NOT fire at CLDLIQ lev 21, q_after = 2.0454743165953276e-28), and the geopotential recompute (geopotential_temp.F90 non-lagrangian branch, hkl = pdel/pmid) asserted via zm_after/s_after against the convect_shallow dump. cld_min_nz = 1 because the site's proc name zm_conv_tend is in cldlim_names (physics_types.F90:246-247).",
